#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Arcsine Integral by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77e5da2-41a6-5747-8bf6-ce061656b42d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291574} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce1119b-3908-54d7-85f2-671cc1186580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291575} {:answer/id #uuid "a3482f5d-bce5-5c29-882a-cfa3432ec756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291576} {:answer/id #uuid "e96a6ce2-eefc-5350-9afc-1fc349551f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291577} {:answer/id #uuid "8011dd0b-6f93-52f0-be2c-df2da4e582e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e96a6ce2-eefc-5350-9afc-1fc349551f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291577} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2683787-d1f3-57a7-9a62-1b306bac0cfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b9411ac-ea97-5e1c-9757-3b199c7513a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-270043" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x-{x}^{2} & =1-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =1-({x}^{2}+2x+1-1) \\\\  & =1-((x+1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2-(x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2(1-(x+1)^{2}/2)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+1)^{2}/(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-1-\\sqrt{2}/2$ | $-1+\\sqrt{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1/2$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1+2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u. \\\\  & =14{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =14\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =14(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =14(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =\\frac{14\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d1dc808-1ee6-5037-b53e-9e1e4686a11c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Arcsecant Integral by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c1ba5e8-56a7-56c6-a719-0e74f223e78a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291581} {:answer/id #uuid "d66372c1-338b-5f5d-91ca-97a24d50562a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c1ba5e8-56a7-56c6-a719-0e74f223e78a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291581} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa43e869-ffd8-534e-bab9-31a347265593" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a0a72f7-fdec-5ce0-ade3-a046bfe26695" :question/math-academy-id "q-348532" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=12{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4+\\sqrt{2}$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =12(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa497df-853e-5e77-9d43-6183fa53ffff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Arctangent Integral by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042725ef-c815-51c0-bee5-0d7e7a31f3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "042725ef-c815-51c0-bee5-0d7e7a31f3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291585} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bcb229c-b6e9-5f9a-ad69-0deda754e10f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8bcf7d0-5de5-553f-a324-8d00997d674e" :question/math-academy-id "q-348553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+10 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $\\sqrt{3}-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa497df-853e-5e77-9d43-6183fa53ffff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Arctangent Integral by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d2c68fa-52b1-5869-97a5-3d4180d88f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\arctan (\\frac{x - 2}{\\sqrt{3}}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066756} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5d2533-4a04-5497-b4f6-f9a9145c77c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\arctan (x - 2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066757} {:answer/id #uuid "c50440a2-1fa8-57df-8cc8-3e59dc724bd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\arctan (\\frac{x - 2}{3}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066758} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbf2ce4-2192-5b3a-b50e-20c53807684c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\arctan (x + 2) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066759} {:answer/id #uuid "5e562131-31b0-53e7-a60a-8fc7ff7ad8b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\arctan (\\frac{x + 2}{\\sqrt{3}}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c68fa-52b1-5869-97a5-3d4180d88f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\arctan (\\frac{x - 2}{\\sqrt{3}}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066756} :answer-field/id #uuid "1472165b-e186-57ef-aa6f-ea1a29860f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87d8f51d-ee05-5977-8eb0-8be27f9cb800" :question/math-academy-id "q-3596" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+7 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+7 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-4+7 \\\\  & =(x-2)^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Arcsine Integral by Completing the Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c76b7bb-5703-55ca-8b4c-e73f92ae4c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291588} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd58941-c2c6-554d-a0e9-8b28c1443d18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+11}{\\sqrt{3}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291589} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ff6f25-d1d8-55eb-b328-8d2b7c6b8388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291590} {:answer/id #uuid "1bbb7a7f-19c2-50a4-8450-2ebf6d3b5c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291591} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd5663b-3b3d-5e09-ae35-bf44c00519b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{11})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c76b7bb-5703-55ca-8b4c-e73f92ae4c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291588} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5cbb3a-5475-593b-988d-5f986996eea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05179cbf-a52b-578c-91d6-1ae5539de82e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49934" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-18x+6 & =-3({x}^{2}+6x-2) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+[{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}]-2) \\\\  & =-3({(x+3)}^{2}-11) \\\\  & =3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33(1-(x+3)^{2}/11)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+3)^{2}/11}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}).$  \n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
